  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Vandeikya/Adikpo HBC</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims at providing a comprehensive range of care and support to about 1000 people living with HIV and AIDS (PLWHA) in rural communities of Vandeikya and Adikpo
The project will carry out community mobilisation activities to raise awareness on HIV/AIDS and tuberculosis. Technical competence of project staff shall be enhanced through capacity building in increasing community behavioural change using stepping-stones training and voluntary counselling and testing (VCT). Counselling, food supply and material support to PLWHA is a core activity of this project. Other support and care activities include referral of clients for anti retroviral drugs, treatment of opportunistic infections, and home visits by volunteers to those clients who are very ill.
Towards the sustainability of the project, CAFOD&#x2019;s grant will be reduced by 20% per annum, and CAFOD&#x2019;s support to the project will include assistance with the development of a strategy for long-term sustainability.</narrative>
  </description>
